`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`
- The design stays safe even with a loose confirmation timing because the leader stays a zombie until it is reaped, so a second observation can't go stale. What actually catches unsafe cases is the post-reap `killpg(pgid, 0)` check, which accepts only ESRCH as proof the group is gone. EPERM there means "can't tell", so a live member that can't be signaled still fails cleanup.
- Since the child was started with `start_new_session=True`, its process group ID equals its PID. While the zombie leader is unreaped, no other process can be given that PID or group ID. That is why being the parent that owns the `waitid` result can stand in for `getpgid`.
